:"higher in AD","module_padj":0.726304,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Microglia","gene_id":"ENSG00000102445","module":"yellow","kme":0.271288,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.554841,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false},"mathys2019":{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000102445"],"dataset_symbols":["KIAA0226L"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/KIAA0226L","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"KIAA0226L","gene_symbol_current":"RUBCNL","gene_id":"ENSG00000102445","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.995087,"donor_log2fc":-0.0292598,"donor_lfcse":0.168728,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.08093e-06},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_symbol":"KIAA0226L","gene_symbol_current":"RUBCNL","gene_id":"ENSG00000102445","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.737032,"nucleus_log2fc":0.155664,"nucleus_score":0.761776,"pct_ad":0.146371,"pct_control":0.132335,"donor_test":"not tested","donor_padj":null,"donor_log2fc":null,"donor_lfcse":null,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000102445","module":"brown","kme":0.192728,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.372712,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000102445","entrez_id":["80183"],"uniprot":["Q9H714"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a cysteine-rich protein that contains a putative zinc-RING and/or ribbon domain. The encoded protein is related to Run domain Beclin-1-interacting and cysteine-rich domain-containing protein, which plays a role in endocytic trafficking and autophagy. In cervical cancer cell lines, this gene is expressed at low levels and may function as a tumor suppressor. Promoter hypermethylation of this gene is observed in cervical cancer cell lines and tissue derived from human patients. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2017].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H714","text":"Regulator of autophagy that promotes autophagosome maturation by facilitating the biogenesis of phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PtdIns(3)P) in late steps of autophagy (PubMed:28306502, PubMed:30704899). Acts by antagonizing RUBCN, thereby stimulating phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase activity of the PI3K/PI3KC3 complex (PubMed:28306502). Following anchorage to the autophagosomal SNARE STX17, promotes the recruitment of PI3K/PI3KC3 and HOPS complexes to the autophagosome to regulate the fusion specificity of autophagosomes with late endosomes/lysosomes (PubMed:28306502). Binds phosphoinositides phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PtdIns(3)P), 4-phosphate (PtdIns(4)P) and 5-phosphate (PtdIns(5)P) (PubMed:28306502). In addition to its role in autophagy, acts as a regulator of lipid and glycogen homeostasis (By similarity). May act as a tumor suppressor (Probable)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}